//  PETPORTS -- LAVA BLOCK MODULE EFFECT
//
//  The status effect half of the lava module. Its script grants lavaImmunity and
//  fireStatusImmunity; see the .lua for why fireResistance, which vanilla pairs
//  with them, is left out.
//
//  THIS IS ONLY HALF THE MODULE, same as poison block. A status effect stops
//  lava hurting a unit that is already standing in it. It cannot get the unit
//  there -- the petport refuses to deploy into a liquid the chassis avoids, and
//  it decides that with no unit in the world to carry an effect. The other half
//  is petports_moduleLiquids on the item.
//
//  NO icon AND NO label. Those drive the status bar on a PLAYER; this is held by
//  a monster under a persistent category, where nothing draws them.
//
//  defaultDuration IS UNREAD ON THE PATH WE USE -- the port applies this with
//  status.setPersistentEffects, which holds it for as long as it is in the set.
//  Stated anyway so an effect applied some other way later does not expire
//  instantly. Same reasoning as petports_module_light and _poisonblock.

{
	"name" : "petports_module_lavablock",

	"effectConfig" : {},

	"defaultDuration" : 60,

	"scripts" : [
		"petports_module_lavablock.lua"
	]
}
